{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778109465,"nonce":"Dpfgxf0j3nzK2dCascda7QR9maw=","title":"Promote coordination-issue scaffolding to a Mandible feature: cross-project templates","message":"We've prototyped a project-coordination protocol in rlrmp using four `coordination`-labeled issues. Cross-project consistency is the next step; Mandible is the natural home.\n\n## Background\n\nIn rlrmp we've established:\n- **Four coordination issues**: analyses (`4d38c15`), training-methods (`c99ad9d`), phases (`b33e8da`), meta cross-project (`1d9ae6f`).\n- **`coordination` label** with auto-close-skip behavior implemented in mandible `34e6e9c` (merged via `5c35dc17`).\n- **Umbrella-verbosity directive** (rlrmp `1ba096f`): higher-level coord/umbrella bodies are minimal + cross-refs.\n- **`## Issue Coordination` section** in project CLAUDE.md documenting the protocol for agents (rlrmp `bcb2205` in flight).\n\nIf we start a new empirical-research project, we want to bootstrap this structure quickly without manually filing four issues + copying CLAUDE.md text.\n\n## User need (per surfacer)\n\n\u003e \"if we create a new project then we might want a very similar setup. And in some sense it's like a template I guess... improve Mandible so that we have this kind of like organization across projects.\"\n\n## Possible feature shapes\n\n### Option A — `mandible project init` (scaffold) [recommended MVP]\n\n```\nmandible project init --template empirical-research\n```\n\nEffect:\n1. Creates the coordination issues (with template-specified titles + bodies, parameterized by project name).\n2. Writes/appends a `## Issue Coordination` section to the project's CLAUDE.md if not already present.\n3. Returns the issue IDs.\n\nConfigurable templates:\n- `empirical-research` — 4 coord axes (analyses, training-methods, phases, meta).\n- `library` — lighter (phases + meta).\n- `application` — phases + meta + custom feature-tracking.\n- `custom --coord \u003cnames\u003e...` — explicit picklist.\n\nTemplates ship as YAML/JSON config in mandible's source tree (e.g., `templates/empirical-research.yml`) so new templates can be added without code changes.\n\n### Option B — First-class coordination CLI\n\n`mandible coord new \u003caxis\u003e`, `mandible coord show`, `mandible coord comment \u003caxis\u003e -m \"...\"`. Coordination becomes a first-class Mandible concept; the underlying git-bug issues are an implementation detail. Heavier; v2.\n\n### Option C — CLAUDE.md template repository in dotfiles\n\nShip a canonical CLAUDE.md fragment that any project can include. Less Mandible-y, more pure-config. Compatible with Option A.\n\n### Option D — Cross-project rendering\n\n`mandible coord list --axis analyses --all-projects` finds every analyses-coord issue across all repos. Useful for portfolio-level views; doesn't help with new-project scaffolding.\n\n## Recommendation\n\n**Option A as MVP.** Concrete, low-effort, preserves git-bug as the underlying tracker, just adds scaffolding. Option B (first-class CLI) and Option D (cross-project listing) are reasonable v2 features once the template is in active use across 2+ projects.\n\n## Concrete first step (if Option A approved)\n\n- Add `mandible project init` subcommand.\n- Ship 1-2 templates initially (`empirical-research`, plus a minimal default).\n- Implement: read template YAML → create issues with template-rendered bodies (substituting project name, repo path) → write CLAUDE.md section if absent (or print it for user to paste if `--no-write-claude-md`).\n- Test: dry-run mode that prints what would be created without actually creating.\n\n## Cross-refs\n\n- rlrmp `1d9ae6f` (meta coord) — surfaced this concern.\n- rlrmp `4d38c15`, `c99ad9d`, `b33e8da`, `1d9ae6f` — the four coord issues that comprise the empirical-research template content.\n- rlrmp `1ba096f` — umbrella-verbosity directive (template should embed this guidance in every coord-issue body it creates).\n- rlrmp `bcb2205` — comprehensive CLAUDE.md `## Issue Coordination` section (template should produce this).\n- mandible `34e6e9c` — coord-label-skip-auto-close (the behavior that makes this whole protocol viable).\n\nLabel: `feature`.","files":null}]}